.SH NAME
messq-doctor - diagnose configuration and operations in prose


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmessq doctor [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Run opinionated health checks over a running daemon (--addr) or an offline data directory (--data-dir) and print prose findings with exact fix commands.

.PP
Checks are pure functions over one collected snapshot; anything they cannot see is reported as [skip] with a reason, never silently omitted. An unreachable daemon is itself a fail finding — doctor is designed to run when things are already broken, so it never exits 6.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--backup-dir\fP=""
	enables the backup.* checks against this directory

.PP
\fB--backup-max-age\fP="168h"
	age at which backup.stale fires

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	offline source: diagnose this data directory read-only

.PP
\fB--explain\fP=""
	print the teaching paragraph for one check id

.PP
\fB--fail-on\fP="warn"
	what makes the exit code 1: info|warn|fail|never

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for doctor

.PP
\fB--idle-after\fP="24h"
	threshold for the consumer.idle* checks

.PP
\fB--list\fP[=false]
	print the registered checks and their summaries

.PP
\fB--only\fP=[]
	comma-separated check ids or family globs to include

.PP
\fB--since\fP="1h"
	analysis window for event- and metric-derived checks

.PP
\fB--skip\fP=[]
	comma-separated check ids or family globs to exclude


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--addr\fP="unix:///run/messq/messq.sock"
	daemon address (unix://, http://, https://)

.PP
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	colour: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--full-ids\fP[=false]
	print full ULIDs instead of abbreviated ones

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="auto"
	output mode: auto|table|json|ndjson

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress narration; data and errors unaffected

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	per-request deadline (0 = none)

.PP
\fB--token-file\fP=""
	file holding the bearer token, mode 0600

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	narrate (-vv dumps each HTTP exchange and the resolved config)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  messq doctor
  messq doctor --data-dir /var/lib/messq --fail-on warn --quiet
  messq doctor --list
  messq doctor --explain storage.wal_size
.EE


